      "id": 1,
      "text": "Gateway's roots stretch back thousands of years, when Athabascan peoples like the Dena'ina and Ahtna hunted, fished, and traded along the Matanuska and Susitna rivers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/gateway_alaska",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The landscape around Gateway rolls gently, with wetlands and low hills drained by streams such as Wasilla Creek, echoing the valley's glacial past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/gateway_alaska",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Elevations in Gateway range from about 200 feet near the valley floor to roughly 1,000 feet on surrounding hills, creating diverse topography.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/gateway_alaska",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Crevasse Moraine Trail System offers 6.7 miles of paths winding through glacial ridges, forested loops, and snowy slopes for year‑round hiking and snowshoeing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/gateway_alaska",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Gateway experiences a subarctic climate, with long, cold winters and short, cool summers typical of the Dfc Köppen classification.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/gateway_alaska",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Named for its position, Gateway serves as a literal gateway to Alaska's rugged interior, bridging suburban life with wilderness adventures.",
